cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "crystal-bci: crystallization-learned templates for fail-closed biosignal commands (SYNTHETIC)"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Brisson"
    given-names: "Jean-François"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-9778-5374"
    affiliation: "Spark AI NLP, Fredericton, New Brunswick, Canada"
version: 0.1.0
license: AGPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/sparkainlp-x/crystal-bci"
abstract: >-
  SYNTHETIC. Applies membrane-crystallization findings to biosignal
  commands: a peak-triggered Hebbian learner extracts a blink template
  (the crystal) unsupervised from a noisy synthetic multichannel stream,
  and a Youden-calibrated fail-closed gate turns blinks into a 'next'
  command. Multi-seed measurements (20 seeds): mean cosine about 0.67,
  mean hit rate about 0.96; the learned crystal beats a fixed template
  on average, while seed-7 perfect rates are above the mean. Synthetic
  signals only; not a medical device; not evaluated on human recordings;
  the device-data adapter is still missing.
keywords:
  - "synthetic-biosignal"
  - "hebbian-learning"
  - "spike-triggered-average"
  - "fail-closed-gate"
  - "brain-computer-interface"
  - "classical-simulation"
  - "synthetic"
